# Hostinger VPS demo deploy

When the user says to add/publish/deploy a project to the VPS ("VPSe ekle", "sunucuya at", "yayınla"), deploy a static build as a subdirectory on the existing demo hub.

## Credentials

Use Cloud Agent secrets already injected as environment variables. Never print, log, or commit them.

- `VPS_HOST` (required)
- `VPS_USER` (default `root`)
- `VPS_PORT` (default `22`)
- `VPS_SSH_PASSWORD` (password auth; alias `VPS_PASSWORD`)
- `VPS_SSH_PRIVATE_KEY` (optional; prefer if set)
- `VPS_DEPLOY_ROOT` (default `/var/www/demos`)

## Target

Nginx serves `/var/www/demos` at `http://$VPS_HOST/`. Each project is:

`/var/www/demos/<slug>/` → `http://$VPS_HOST/<slug>/`

Existing demos include `anaokulu` and `satiskolay`. The hub listing is `/var/www/demos/index.html`.

## How to deploy

Run `scripts/vps-deploy.sh` (also installed as `vps-deploy` after environment setup):

```bash
scripts/vps-deploy.sh --source ./dist --slug my-demo --title "Demo Title" --description "Kısa açıklama"
```

- Pick a URL-safe lowercase slug (`[a-z0-9-]`).
- Deploy the built static files, not `.git` or `.env`.
- Let the script update the hub `index.html` unless the user asks not to.
- After deploy, fetch `http://$VPS_HOST/<slug>/` and confirm the page loads.

Do not use root credentials from chat, README, or committed files.
